          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"dumas-fils-la-dame-aux-camelias-47275cd93e72e11f\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.96,\"analysis\":\"Armand directly avows that he loves Marguerite, emphasizing the exceptional degree of his feeling through comparison with everyone who has loved her before. The utterance presents a loving emotional state as true. Although it occurs during courtship and is intended to influence her, it does not itself undertake a commitment. Its emotional intensity remains part of an emphatic avowal rather than independently evidenced expressive/reflexive discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The courtship setting creates slight pragmatic pressure toward a relational undertaking, but no commitment is encoded or clearly enacted by this particular sentence.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Direct speech by the first-person narrator, Armand, to Marguerite within the narrated conversation.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Armand answers Marguerite’s criticism of his premature jealousy by claiming that his love is unprecedented. His earlier narration reveals both genuine emotional disturbance and a strategic wish to gain influence over her, but calculation and persuasive purpose do not alter the core force from a strong avowal. Marguerite understands it as such, asking whether he truly loves her so much and how long the feeling has lasted. The subsequent negotiation of terms for becoming lovers is contextually important but distinct from any undertaking made by this sentence itself.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"« C'est que personne ne vous a jamais aimée comme je vous aime. »\",\"supports\":\"The explicit present-tense first-person love predicate, intensified by comparison with all previous lovers, strongly supports truth-conditional avowal.\",\"confidence\":1.0},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Marguerite responds: « Voyons, franchement, vous m'aimez donc bien? » Armand answers: « Autant qu'il est possible d'aimer, je crois. »\",\"supports\":\"The addressee’s uptake and Armand’s elaboration treat the occurrence as a claim about the existence and degree of his loving state.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Armand says his love has lasted since seeing Marguerite three years earlier.\",\"supports\":\"The asserted duration further frames the love language as a report or avowal of an enduring emotional state.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The later promises and conditions—« si vous me promettez de faire toutes mes volontés » and « je serai tout ce que vous voudrez »—occur separately from the highlighted sentence.\",\"supports\":\"The passage distinguishes the highlighted avowal from the explicit relational undertakings that follow, weighing against substantial performative force in the core occurrence.\",\"confidence\":0.96},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The narration describes Armand as deeply hurt and says Marguerite overwhelms him, while also noting his desire to « prendre d'empire » over her.\",\"supports\":\"The utterance is emotionally and strategically situated, but neither intensity nor persuasive calculation independently establishes expressive/reflexive or performative core force.\",\"confidence\":0.94}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core as an emphatic avowal of love. Its strategic, jealous, and courtship functions belong to contextual interpretation and create no residual core force requiring E or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":\"The supplied translation was treated only as an analytical aid; the classification is grounded in the French source context.\"}"
        }
